# Game Development .gitignore Addendum
#
# Append the block for your engine to the repository root .gitignore.
#
# This file is an example addendum. It is NOT active in this repository.
# The starter's own .gitignore intentionally contains only generic OS and
# local-only entries; engine-specific ignores belong here so they do not leak
# into non-game repositories.

# --- Phaser / web-game projects (Vite, or any bundler) ---
# node_modules/
# dist/
# dist-ssr/
# .vite/
# *.local
#
# # Editor and tooling
# .vscode/*
# !.vscode/extensions.json
# .idea/
# *.tsbuildinfo
#
# # Generated runtime assets, when the pipeline rebuilds them
# app/game/assets/runtime/generated/
#
# # Never commit real credentials or signing material
# .env
# .env.*
# !.env.example
# *.keystore
# *.jks
# *.p12
# *.pfx
# *.mobileprovision

# --- Unity (only if the repo contains a Unity project) ---
# [Ll]ibrary/
# [Tt]emp/
# [Oo]bj/
# [Bb]uild/
# [Bb]uilds/
# [Ll]ogs/
# [Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
# *.csproj
# *.sln
# *.unityproj
# .vs/

# --- Unreal (only if the repo contains an Unreal project) ---
# Binaries/
# DerivedDataCache/
# Intermediate/
# Saved/
# .vs/
# *.VC.db

# --- Godot (only if the repo contains a Godot project) ---
# .godot/
# export_presets.cfg

# --- Notes ---
# 1. Keep engine blocks commented out until that engine is actually present.
# 2. Never uncomment a line that ignores prebuilt binaries the project ships intentionally.
# 3. Do not gitignore lockfiles (package-lock.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, yarn.lock).
#    They must be committed so builds stay reproducible.
# 4. Store real credentials in a secret manager or CI secrets, never in .env.
